DeployCheckActionTest
├── when the action names the manager and the pin
│   └── it should pass
├── when the action was deployed with another manager
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name the expected and the actual manager
├── when the action names another deployed manager
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name the expected and the actual manager
├── when the action names the zero manager
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name the expected and the actual manager
├── when the action was deployed with another implementation
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name the expected and the actual implementation
├── when the action names the zero implementation
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name the expected and the actual implementation
├── when the pin differs from the action's implementation
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name the pin as expected and the action's implementation as actual
├── when the action address holds a contract without the actions views
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name recoveryAction and the address in the read failure
├── when the action answers no bytes
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name recoveryAction and the address in the read failure
├── when the action answers a word with bits above an address
│   ├── it should revert
│   └── it should name recoveryAction and the address in the read failure
└── when the implementation read fails
    ├── it should revert
    └── it should name recoveryAction and the address in the read failure
